.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-spectwarp 1  "pvc-spectwarp " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-spectwarp \- Per\-bin dynamics processor: compresses or expands each bin\*(Aqs amplitude relative to its *own frame\*(Aqs* live spectral peak (a self\-referential envelope\-follower), within an adjustable frequency band
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-spectwarp\fR [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-stretch\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-compress\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-compress\-amount\fR] [\fB\-\-expand\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-expand\-amount\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-band\-rolloff\fR] [\fB\-\-warp\-curve\fR] [\fB\-\-response\-time\fR] [\fB\-\-complement\fR] [\fB\-\-compress\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-normalize\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Per\-bin dynamics processor: compresses or expands each bin\*(Aqs amplitude relative to its *own frame\*(Aqs* live spectral peak (a self\-referential envelope\-follower), within an adjustable frequency band.
.PP
Ports `spectwarper`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ spectwarper.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::spectwarper`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope, including a real bound bug in the original tool\*(Aqs sliding\-window mode, reproduced faithfully.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]
FFT size (must be a power of two)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 2048]
Analysis/resynthesis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`); the C\*(Aqs own hardcoded default is a literal `2048`, matching `pv`\*(Aqs `\-\-window\-size` gotcha
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-\-stretch\fR \fI<STRETCH>\fR [default: 1]
Time\-stretch factor (`1.0` = unchanged)
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fI<PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
Pitch shift in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
Frequency shift in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\-threshold\fR \fI<COMPRESS_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
Compression threshold in dB, relative to the live peak \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\-amount\fR \fI<COMPRESS_AMOUNT>\fR [default: 0]
Compression amount in dB (must be negative to actually compress \- a non\-negative value is a no\-op in the real tool) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\-threshold\fR \fI<EXPAND_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-96]
Expansion threshold in dB (clamped to `>= \-95` in the real tool) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-expand\-amount\fR \fI<EXPAND_AMOUNT>\fR [default: 0]
Expansion amount in dB (must be negative to actually expand) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-band\-low\fR \fI<BAND_LOW>\fR [default: 0]
Companding band low edge in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-band\-high\fR \fI<BAND_HIGH>\fR [default: \-1]
Companding band high edge in Hz (`< 0` = Nyquist) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-band\-rolloff\fR \fI<BAND_ROLLOFF>\fR [default: 0]
Companding band rolloff width in octaves \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-warp\-curve\fR \fI<WARP_CURVE>\fR [default: 0]
Shape exponent for the compress/expand gradient curve (`0` = linear) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-response\-time\fR \fI<RESPONSE_TIME>\fR [default: 0]
Smoothing time in seconds for the per\-bin amplitude\-change multiplier \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-complement\fR \fI<COMPLEMENT>\fR [default: 0]
Proportion (`0..1`) of the unmodified source blended back into the companded result \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\-window\fR \fI<COMPRESS_WINDOW>\fR [default: 0]
Sliding compression window size (`<= 0` = one global peak for the whole band; `<= 8` = octaves, `> 8` = Hz) \- a plain number, or `@path`. See `pvc\-core::tools::spectwarper`\*(Aqs doc comment for a real bound bug in the original tool this triggers
.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
Peak\-reference attack time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
Peak\-reference release time in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\-limit\fR \fI<NORMALIZE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
Per\-frame amplitude normalization limit in dB (`0` disables normalization) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
Low shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
High shelf EQ gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
Low shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
High shelf EQ frequency in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-threshold\fR \fI<THRESHOLD>\fR [default: \-96]
Oscillator resynthesis threshold in dB (bins quieter than this, relative to the frame\*(Aqs own peak, are skipped)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

